<p>Greek police arrested an 89-year-old man Tuesday after shootings at a social security office and a court building in central Athens wounded five people, Greece&#x27;s state broadcaster ERT and authorities cited by several agencies said. Police said the suspect was armed with a shotgun and first opened fire at a social security office, wounding an employee, before a second shooting at a courthouse injured others. Authorities detained the suspect hours later in Patras, about 200 km west of Athens, after a nationwide search; some reports said he was near transport links and may have been trying to leave Greece. The motive was not formally established, but ERT reported the gunman left envelopes containing documents at the courthouse, and several reports said he had grievances connected to pension payments.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/FxRGdv1FLF84ekAVpf26gx7TKTBlnLiKU5fuDRvmdK_uyvrjGO55jM2dm9FlWJB8ecjFjm6RcuPvd6DWKqt0Ww7bk-AK2cMV8Ci1nvFemrtqm1g2MAWslPSl-3tS2to-ZfgoJhy1aQpOxoJNBLflGklDhGhaZmvYo1JQgdR6l2uBoCE-tOuN5sua1c_PX_zLtXabWNhUTcwofLv6Hx0cmB2Ny6HnYltR39BaHY6VtFWd-zinzDn8XQsYKDCO04v7AdQl5gXeKUK9pgbhO6TGBL3swAwB' alt='A policeman speaks to a woman outside a court building.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Security screening: ABC reported that the attacker entered the social security office with a shotgun hidden in the sleeve of a trench coat and passed through security undetected.</li><li>Court injuries: Stratis Dounias, head of the Athens Judicial Employees Union, said initial information indicated the shooter fired at the floor, and court employees were slightly wounded by ricocheting shotgun pellets.</li><li>Weapons seized: Police found the shotgun after the courthouse shooting, and media reports said the suspect had a loaded revolver when arrested.</li><li>Security footage: Local television aired security-camera images showing a man walking calmly near the social security office while carrying what appeared to be a short-barreled shotgun.</li></ul